my class went to a local vet's office we  got to see the exam rooms and play with  some puppies then they took us to an  operating room and brought in a cat we  watch them and necess eyes the cat shave  its stomach and slice its belly open to  prepare to spay it I don't know what  happened next because I passed out we  went to an indoor trampoline park but  didn't get to bounce on anything just  got to listen to the owner talk about  what it's like to own a business my  class had to go to a funeral parlor we  wrote our own obituaries picked out  coffins and practiced mourning my fourth  grade class took a trip to a plantation  house to learn more about Georgia's  history it was really nice and authentic  but there was one activity where they  slipped the class up to do different  things they made all the people of color  go out in the field and pick cotton  while all the white kids got to play  dress-up in the house our field trip was  to the back of the school we sat on the  asphalt listening to someone explained  to us what the different numbers on  plastic containers meant we went on a  field trip to a dairy farm we got to  help milk the cows and help feed the  calves the next step on the trip was an  abattoir where we watched the cows  unloaded killed and then went to the  room where they cut out the bones after  that we went to lunch where we were  served beef pies it was not a  well-planned day
 

